    {
      "predicate": "iadas:limites",
      "object": "The present study was limited by the self-report nature of the surveys and the willingness of athletes to honestly and accurately respond to survey items. The results are also based on a convenience sample of skaters limited to clubs in the Midwest and Northeast. A random and more representative sample of skaters nationally and internationally, inclusive of males, should be considered in future research. Using a cross-sectional design, causal relationships and change over time could not be determined. Future research would benefit from longitudinal designs and multivariate analyses to identify risk factors of disordered eating in figure skaters and more directly test the relationships proposed in Petrie and Greenleaf's (2012) theoretical model."
    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:perspectives",
      "object": "Future research should address the instrument's psychometric properties and the conceptual differences between positive and negative perfectionism. It should also explore the relationship between athletic identity and disordered eating in the context of their specific sport environment. Additionally, longitudinal designs and multivariate analyses should be used to identify risk factors of disordered eating in figure skaters and more directly test the relationships proposed in Petrie and Greenleaf's (2012) theoretical model."
